# Build context for trainer/Dockerfile. The context is the repository root
# because the image installs the `medos` package from it; everything that is not that
# package, the trainer, or `pyproject.toml` is excluded, so a rebuild is not invalidated
# by a test run or a downloaded fixture.
#
# `.git` IS EXCLUDED ON PURPOSE. The commit reaches the image as a build argument that
# `trainer/build.sh` reads from git on the host, never as a repository the image
# could re-interrogate. An image that can run `git rev-parse` is an image that can report
# a commit for a tree it was not built from.
*
!medos/medos/
!pyproject.toml
!trainer/

# ...and inside those, the things that are never part of the image.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
trainer/build.sh
trainer/README.md
# The trainer's own suite moved here from `tests/` when the tree did. It is not in the
# image -- the Dockerfile copies `medos_trainer/` and the bindings file by name, never the
# directory -- but it IS in the build context, and this file's whole purpose is that
# editing a test does not invalidate a layer.
trainer/tests/
